## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Import-time side effects**: Multiple modules execute heavy operations at import time:
> - `ingestion_tasks.py` L25-28: creates a live `redis.from_url()` client and loads `SentenceTransformer` model
> - `redis_repo_sync.py` L10-19: creates a live Redis client at module scope (raises `ValueError` if `REDIS_URL` unset)
> - `retriever.py` L12-20: creates a `ChromaDB CloudClient` at module scope
> - `query_embedding.py` L4-6: loads `SentenceTransformer` at module scope
>
> The test suite will use `unittest.mock.patch` and environment variable stubs to prevent these from executing during tests. Modules with unavoidable import-time side effects will be patched **before** the importing module is loaded.

> [!WARNING]
> **Celery ALWAYS_EAGER**: The ingestion pipeline uses `workflow.apply_async()` with a Celery `chain()`. In `ALWAYS_EAGER` mode, this runs synchronously but still requires a Redis-backed broker to be configured. The test conftest will configure the Celery app with `task_always_eager=True` and set `broker_url` / `result_backend` to `"memory://"` to avoid needing a real Redis instance.

> [!NOTE]
> **The `redis_repo_sync.py` module** raises `ValueError` at import time if `REDIS_URL` is not set. The health endpoint imports this. Tests will set `REDIS_URL` as an env var in conftest and provide a `fakeredis` instance via monkeypatching.

